lynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-3X+5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-3X+5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-3D+5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-3D+5I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-3+5 & -3+9+0 \\\\ -1+3+0 & 3+0+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1069 "q-279420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find ${A}^{2}.$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${A}^{2}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49538b11-2cc9-55ec-b3f4-d0592d2d086e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486379 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${A}^{2},$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486381 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486381 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486381 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486381 #edb/ref 1071 "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${B}^{2}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486381 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d7d778d-4fa7-5799-8edf-5efbc5ed3cdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486381 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${B}^{2},$ we multiply $B$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -8 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1069 "q-279444" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find ${B}^{2}.$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\">${B}^{2}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-5}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ccd2400f-e477-5772-b36d-b9c99ce24efe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486443 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${B}^{2},$ we multiply $B$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486453 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486453 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486453 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486453 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486453 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ebea1a9b-d1dc-56a2-8933-0092e4727688" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486453 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X-1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X-I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+A-I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+A-I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+3-1 & 0-2+0 \\\\ 0+4+0 & 1-3-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
